      "result": "Implemented the persistent URL shortener API. It uses PostgreSQL with Alembic migrations, preserves submitted URLs, validates request data, handles duplicate codes, and increments click counts with a single atomic database update.\n\n`sh start.sh` applies migrations and starts the server on `0.0.0.0:8000`. The startup instructions are in the README.\n\nVerified the endpoints against PostgreSQL, including creation, duplicate codes, listing, redirects and click tracking, missing links, and invalid or malformed requests. The only check output was a deprecation warning from Starlette’s test client; the checks passed.",
